<title>POLAND: Polish meat firm wants bourse entry H2 1997.</title>
<headline>Polish meat firm wants bourse entry H2 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish meat-processing firm Zaklady Miesne Pozmeat SA wants to enter the Warsaw bourse in the second half of 1997 and plans an initial public offering in April, an official from the brokerage offering the shares said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The public offering is planned for April and the bourse debut in July or August,&quot; Maciej Wadzel of BMT brokerage told Reuters, adding that Pozmeat was seeking a parallel market listing.</p>
<p>Pozmeat had a net profit of 0.1 million zlotys on 114.3 million zloty sales in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Barbara Wozniak +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
